          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The temperature difference between a cup of coffee and its surroundings decreases by 25% every 5 minutes. The coffee is initially 60 degrees hotter than its surroundings; this can be modelled by ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "D=60(0.75)^t",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " where ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "t",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is the number of 5 minute periods. After how long will it take for the temperature difference to be less than 5°C? Answer to the nearest whole minute.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "43 min (threshold rounded to the nearest whole minute)\n\nSolve the decay inequality using logarithms, reversing the sign for a base below 1, then convert five-minute intervals to minutes.",
      "worked": "Here $t\\geq0$ counts five-minute periods.\n$$\\begin{align*}60(0.75)^t &< 5\\\\(0.75)^t &< \\frac{1}{12}\\\\t &> \\log_{0.75}\\left(\\frac{1}{12}\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nTaking logarithms to base $0.75$ reverses the inequality because $0<0.75<1$. For elapsed time $m=5t$ in minutes,\n$$m>5\\log_{0.75}\\left(\\frac{1}{12}\\right).$$\nThe threshold is approximately 43.1884 minutes, which rounds to 43 minutes as requested. The first whole minute satisfying the strict inequality is 44 minutes.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 20
  },
